  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14153614/assets/ebd87e37a8f01369e1f62f166879d08a4d2e6cc59a787662a36ec0a297036878.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            Brenda is Dan's neighbor. She has a plot of land whose area is ${x}^{2}-4$ square yards and whose width is $x+2$ yards, as depicted above. What is the length of Brenda's plot in terms of $x?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        Brenda's plot has a length of \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \nyards.",
  "worked_solution": "To find the length of Brenda's plot of land, we need to factor the expression ${x}^{2}-4.$\n\nFirst, we write the expression as a difference of squares:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-4={x}^{2}-{2}^{2}\n$$\n\nThen, we factor the expression using the difference of squares formula:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-{2}^{2}=(x+2)(x-2)\n$$\n\nAs a result, we conclude that the length of the plot must be $x-2$ yards.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14153614/assets/af8ec2bf60ee66fb71ad633dbcd5963bbb4aaa7f670cbfc76f4e2855021c1bf3.png)",
